card.statement:
Let $\pi'$ be a subset of $\pi$, let $\zeta\in Q^+(\pi)$ and $\xi\in Q(\pi)$ and let $g,u$ be nonzero elements of $G^-_{-\zeta},  U^+$ respectively. Either there exists $\alpha_i\in \pi'$ such that

\begin{align}
({\rm ad}\ F_i)gK_{\xi}u\in  g'K_{\xi}u + G_{-\zeta} U^0 U^+
\end{align}

where $g'$ is a nonzero term in $G^-_{-\zeta-\alpha_i}$ or $gK_{\xi}$ is a nonzero $({\rm ad}\ U_{\pi'})$ lowest weight vector. Hence if

\begin{align}
X\in gK_{\xi}u+\sum_{\lambda\not\geq\zeta}G^-_{-\lambda}U^0U^+
\end{align}

where $g\in G_{-\zeta}$ and $X\in \mathcal{N}(\mathcal{B}_{\theta}: \mathcal{B}_{\theta}\cap U_{\pi'})$ then $gK_{\xi}$ is an $({\rm ad}\ U_{\pi'})$ lowest weight vector or $uK_{\xi+\zeta}\in \mathcal{M}^+\mathcal{T}_{\theta}$.
